  "methodology": {
    "calibration": "Each pairwise table was raked to the exact supplied one-way marginals.",
    "caveats": [
      "Every one-way marginal exactly matches the supplied demographic percentages before output rounding.",
      "The full joint tensor is a maximum-entropy/IPF synthesis constrained by the included pairwise distributions; it is not a directly published seven-variable Census table.",
      "The Census sex tables contain Female and Male only. The 2% Other category is modeled and calibrated, so intersections involving Other have lower evidentiary strength.",
      "Income means household income. Income cross-tabs use householder-based ACS tables as structural proxies and interpolate published income brackets to the supplied boundaries.",
      "Party source tables report Democrat/Republican alignment, including leaners. The supplied Democrat, Republican, Independent and Other categories are modeled from the 2026 direct-party/leaner/no-lean composition and then calibrated to the supplied party marginal.",
      "Race/ethnicity output is treated as mutually exclusive and calibrated to the supplied race marginal. Some ACS source iterations are not perfectly mutually exclusive before calibration.",
      "Race-by-education structure is primarily for adults age 25+ because that is the universe of the most detailed ACS race-by-education tables.",
      "These constraints improve realism but do not establish survey representativeness by themselves; synthetic personas remain model-generated observations."
    ]
  }
